Redundant Conditional Check Identified.

Redundant Conditional Check in `collectFeesInEther`
'''
In the `collectFeesInEther` function, the second `if (collectedFees == 0) throw;` condition is redundant. When `_amt > collectedFees`, the preceding `collectAllFees()` call sets `collectedFees` to zero, making the subsequent check always true. When `_amt <= collectedFees`, `collectedFees` cannot be zero because `_amt` is at least 1 ether (after multiplication), so the check is always false. This redundant conditional adds unnecessary complexity and gas cost without altering behavior.

**Mitigation**: Remove the redundant `if (collectedFees == 0) throw;` condition. If the intent is to prevent proceeding after collecting all fees (when `_amt > collectedFees`), replace it with an unconditional `throw` (or `revert`) directly after the `collectAllFees()` call, or restructure the logic to avoid the duplicate check. For example:

```solidity
function collectFeesInEther(uint _amt) onlyowner {
    _amt *= 1 ether;
    if (_amt > collectedFees) {
        collectAllFees();
        throw; // or revert
    }
    // else: _amt <= collectedFees, proceed safely
    creator.send(_amt);
    collectedFees -= _amt;
}
```

This eliminates the redundant condition and clarifies the control flow.
'''
Detector: RedundantConditionalDetector
Classification: code-quality (no standard SWC)
